WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:04.717
- [Narrator] This is
Cami, a red ruffed lemur.

00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:08.279
Her world is small, and
it's shrinking daily.

00:00:08.279 --> 00:00:11.990
(eclectic music)

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.449
The red ruffed lemur comes
by its name, honestly.

00:00:15.449 --> 00:00:18.526
It's covered in a brilliant chestnut coat.

00:00:18.526 --> 00:00:21.301
The rest of its body, its
face, hands, belly, and tail

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:24.099
are a deep black.

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:26.806
Of the hundreds of species
of lemur in Madagascar,

00:00:26.806 --> 00:00:30.617
the red ruffed lemur is
one of the most endangered.

00:00:30.617 --> 00:00:33.440
Found only on a single
peninsula in the north west

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.420
of the island country the
rainforests the red ruffed lemur

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.687
call home are also highly valued
for the beautiful rosewood

00:00:39.687 --> 00:00:42.384
and ebony trees that grow there.

00:00:42.384 --> 00:00:46.502
It's in the canopy of these
that you can find these lemurs.

00:00:46.502 --> 00:00:48.486
There they search for
fruit, which makes up

00:00:48.486 --> 00:00:50.756
nearly their whole diet.

00:00:50.756 --> 00:00:53.969
Their home forests are being
harvested at an alarming rate,

00:00:53.969 --> 00:00:57.913
taking the red ruffed lemur's
chance of survival with them.

00:00:57.913 --> 00:00:59.946
Conservationists estimate
that there are only

00:00:59.946 --> 00:01:03.745
three to 5,000 left in the wild.

00:01:03.745 --> 00:01:07.242
This is the red ruffed lemur.

00:01:07.242 --> 00:01:11.409
(eclectic music)

